### `UserStore.worker_exists(self, worker_id)`

**Algorithm**
1. Read `workers.csv`.
2. Compare each Worker ID case-insensitively with the supplied ID.
3. Return true when a match exists; otherwise return false.

**Flowchart**
```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A([Start]) --> B[Read workers.csv rows]
    B --> C{Matching Worker ID found?}
    C -- Yes --> D[Return true]
    C -- No --> E[Return false]
    D --> F([End])
    E --> F
```

**Pseudocode**
```text
FUNCTION UserStore.worker_exists(worker_id)
    FOR EACH worker in workers.csv
        IF uppercase(trim(worker.ID)) = uppercase(trim(worker_id)) THEN
            RETURN true
        END IF
    END FOR
    RETURN false
END FUNCTION
```

### `UserStore.create_user(self, worker_id, username, password, full_name, title, role)`

**Algorithm**
1. Normalize the Worker ID and username; read existing accounts.
2. Reject missing required fields or passwords shorter than eight characters.
3. Reject IDs not present in the worker table, duplicate Worker IDs or duplicate usernames.
4. Hash the password, append the account, save all accounts and return success.

**Flowchart**
```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A([Start]) --> B[Normalize ID and username; read users]
    B --> C{Required fields complete?}
    C -- No --> X[Return missing-field message]
    C -- Yes --> D{Password at least 8 chars?}
    D -- No --> Y[Return password-length message]
    D -- Yes --> E{Worker ID exists?}
    E -- No --> Z[Return unknown-worker message]
    E -- Yes --> G{Duplicate ID or username?}
    G -- Yes --> Q[Return duplicate message]
    G -- No --> H[Hash password and append account]
    H --> I[Write users.csv]
    I --> J[Return success]
    X --> K([End])
    Y --> K
    Z --> K
    Q --> K
    J --> K
```

**Pseudocode**
```text
FUNCTION UserStore.create_user(worker_id, username, password, full_name, title, role)
    normalize worker_id to uppercase and username to lowercase
    users = read_users()
    IF required values are missing RETURN failure
    IF password length < 8 RETURN failure
    IF worker_id is absent from workers.csv RETURN failure
    IF worker_id or username already exists RETURN failure
    append account with hashed password to users
    write_users(users)
    RETURN success
END FUNCTION
```

### `UserStore.authenticate(self, username, worker_id, password)`

**Algorithm**
1. Read the stored accounts.
2. For each account, compare normalized username and Worker ID.
3. For matching identifiers, check the password hash.
4. Return the public user details for the first valid account; otherwise return `None`.

**Flowchart**
```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A([Start]) --> B[Read accounts]
    B --> C{More accounts?}
    C -- No --> N[Return no match]
    C -- Yes --> D{Username and Worker ID match?}
    D -- No --> C
    D -- Yes --> E{Password hash matches?}
    E -- No --> C
    E -- Yes --> F[Return user details]
    F --> G([End])
    N --> G
```

**Pseudocode**
```text
FUNCTION UserStore.authenticate(username, worker_id, password)
    FOR EACH account in read_users()
        IF normalized identifiers match AND password_matches(password, account.hash) THEN
            RETURN account's username, worker ID, name, title and role
        END IF
    END FOR
    RETURN None
END FUNCTION
```

### `UserStore.update_password(self, worker_id, current_password, new_password)`

**Algorithm**
1. Reject a new password shorter than eight characters.
2. Read accounts and find the account matching the normalized Worker ID.
3. Reject an incorrect current password.
4. Hash and save the new password, then return success.
5. If no account matches, return the not-found result.

**Flowchart**
```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A([Start]) --> B{New password at least 8 chars?}
    B -- No --> X[Return length error]
    B -- Yes --> C[Read accounts and search Worker ID]
    C --> D{Account found?}
    D -- No --> Y[Return not-found error]
    D -- Yes --> E{Current password matches?}
    E -- No --> Z[Return current-password error]
    E -- Yes --> F[Hash new password and save accounts]
    F --> G[Return success]
    X --> H([End])
    Y --> H
    Z --> H
    G --> H
```

**Pseudocode**
```text
FUNCTION UserStore.update_password(worker_id, current_password, new_password)
    IF length(new_password) < 8 RETURN failure
    users = read_users()
    FOR EACH account in users
        IF account.Worker_ID matches worker_id THEN
            IF current password does not match RETURN failure
            replace account password hash
            write_users(users)
            RETURN success
        END IF
    END FOR
    RETURN account-not-found failure
END FUNCTION
```

