### `build_alerts(workers, incidents, equipment_summary, maintenance)`

**Algorithm**
1. For every worker, calculate worker risk and add alerts for PPE non-compliance, high fatigue and High risk score.
2. Add Critical alerts for incidents whose severity is fatal, major or critical.
3. Add Critical or Warning alerts for equipment condition.
4. For every maintenance record, add a High overdue alert when status is overdue or due date has passed; otherwise add a Warning when downtime exceeds 12 hours.
5. Return the accumulated alert dictionaries.

**Flowchart**
```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A([Start]) --> B[Initialize alerts]
    B --> C[Scan workers: PPE, fatigue and risk]
    C --> D[Append matching worker alerts]
    D --> E[Scan incidents for fatal, major or critical]
    E --> F[Append matching incident alerts]
    F --> G[Scan equipment conditions]
    G --> H[Append Critical or Warning equipment alerts]
    H --> I[Scan maintenance records]
    I --> J{Overdue status or past due date?}
    J -- Yes --> K[Append High overdue alert]
    J -- No --> L{Downtime > 12 hours?}
    L -- Yes --> M[Append Warning downtime alert]
    L -- No --> N[No maintenance alert]
    K --> O{More maintenance rows?}
    M --> O
    N --> O
    O -- Yes --> I
    O -- No --> P[Return alerts]
    P --> Q([End])
```

**Pseudocode**
```text
FUNCTION build_alerts(workers, incidents, equipment_summary, maintenance)
    alerts = empty list
    FOR EACH worker
        score, level = worker_risk(worker safety fields)
        add High alert for non-compliant PPE
        add High alert for high fatigue
        add High alert when risk level is High
    END FOR
    FOR EACH incident
        IF lowercase(severity) in fatal, major, critical THEN add Critical alert
    END FOR
    FOR EACH equipment item
        IF condition is Critical THEN add Critical alert
        ELSE IF condition is Warning THEN add Warning alert
    END FOR
    today = current date
    FOR EACH maintenance row
        IF status is overdue OR due date < today THEN add High overdue alert
        ELSE IF downtime > 12 THEN add Warning downtime alert
    END FOR
    RETURN alerts
END FUNCTION
```

